Welcome to Zenix, a small Unix-like system for Amigas
with a 68020 or better.

The whole disk now runs from memory: programs start at once,
the floppy may be taken out, and nothing is ever written to it.
Your files live in memory (about 250 KB of room) until the
Amiga is switched off.

 The icons, the Zenix menu  a shell, Files (Ahiru), Editor
                            (Sumi), Monitor (ctop)
 Amiga+Return  a terminal   Amiga+Q      close a window
 Amiga+Tab     next window  Amiga+Space  the menu
 Amiga+F2..F10 text consoles (log in as guest); Amiga+F1 back
 man demo      what is on this disk; man NAME for a command
 ifconfig      the network (a network card: see man demo)

Press Return to close this window.
